<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Talysh</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Talysh is a historical region on the south-western shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>, divided between south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilan">Gilan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> provinces. Home of the Talysh people, who speak a north-western Iranian language, it has humid forested mountains and fertile lowlands. In the 18th century its northern part formed the Talysh Khanate, which passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> under the treaties of 1813 and 1828.</p></div>
